{
 "ep": 6,
 "total": 140,
 "title": "Cluster, Instance, Database and Schema",
 "phase": "Foundations",
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Cluster, database, schema: don't confuse these.",
   "cap": "*Cluster,* *database,* *schema:* don't confuse these."
  },
  {
   "say": "This is episode six of the PostgreSQL DBA series. Today: four layers every DBA must know.",
   "cap": "Episode 6: the *four* *layers* every DBA must know."
  },
  {
   "say": "Start at the top. A database cluster is a collection of databases, managed by one running server.",
   "cap": "*Cluster:* a collection of databases, one running server.",
   "cue": "cluster"
  },
  {
   "say": "You create it with initdb, and on disk it lives in one data directory, often called PGDATA.",
   "cap": "Created by *initdb.* Lives in one *data* *directory.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "The instance is the running part: the postmaster, its processes and their shared memory.",
   "cap": "*Instance:* postmaster, processes, *shared* *memory.*",
   "cue": "instance"
  },
  {
   "say": "One instance manages exactly one cluster. Several instances can run on one server, if their ports don't conflict.",
   "cap": "One instance, *one* *cluster.* Many instances need *different* *ports.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Inside the cluster live databases, like appdb.",
   "cap": "Inside the cluster live *databases.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "A new cluster already has three: postgres, template1 and template0.",
   "cap": "New cluster: *postgres,* *template1,* *template0.*",
   "cue": "three"
  },
  {
   "say": "Roles, tablespaces and database names are global objects, shared by the whole cluster.",
   "cap": "*Global* *objects:* roles, tablespaces, database names."
  },
  {
   "say": "Inside each database are schemas, and schemas hold the tables, views and functions.",
   "cap": "Databases hold *schemas.* Schemas hold *tables* and *functions.*",
   "cue": "schemas"
  },
  {
   "say": "So the full hierarchy is: cluster, database, schema, table.",
   "cap": "*Cluster* > *database* > *schema* > *table.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Careful: the docs say cluster is sometimes used for the instance. And it's not the CLUSTER command either.",
   "cap": "*Cluster* can mean the instance. Not the *CLUSTER* *command.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Let's check a real server. Select datname from pg_database.",
   "cap": "Live: *datname* from *pg_database.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Five rows: the three defaults, plus appdb and reportdb, which I created for this demo.",
   "cap": "*5* *rows:* 3 defaults + *appdb* and *reportdb.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Now, connected to appdb, list the schemas with backslash d n.",
   "cap": "In appdb: list schemas with *\\dn.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "public comes with every new database, and by default, tables without a schema name go there.",
   "cap": "*public* is in every new database. *Default* home for tables."
  },
  {
   "say": "Common mistake: one connection reaches exactly one database.",
   "cap": "Mistake: one connection reaches *one* *database* only."
  },
  {
   "say": "From appdb, I queried reportdb. PostgreSQL refused: cross-database references are not implemented.",
   "cap": "*ERROR:* cross-database references are *not* *implemented.*",
   "cue": "refused"
  },
  {
   "say": "Schemas are different. From the same connection, billing dot invoices works, if you have the privileges.",
   "cap": "*billing.invoices* works from the same connection.",
   "cue": "invoices"
  },
  {
   "say": "To reach another database, the docs point to foreign data wrappers, such as postgres_fdw.",
   "cap": "Across databases: *foreign* *data* *wrappers* like *postgres_fdw.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Their advice: unrelated projects get separate databases. Related projects can share one, with separate schemas.",
   "cap": "*Unrelated:* separate databases. *Related:* separate schemas.",
   "cue": "Related"
  },
  {
   "say": "DBA takeaway: databases in a cluster share one WAL, so a physical backup covers the whole cluster.",
   "cap": "One *shared* *WAL.* A physical backup is *cluster-wide.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Recap: the cluster is the data, and the instance runs it.",
   "cap": "Recap: *cluster* is the data, *instance* runs it."
  },
  {
   "say": "Databases are isolated, and schemas are namespaces inside them.",
   "cap": "*Databases* are isolated. *Schemas* are namespaces."
  },
  {
   "say": "Next up: what lives inside the PostgreSQL data directory. Follow so you don't miss it, and send this to a friend who's learning PostgreSQL.",
   "cap": "Next up: inside *PGDATA.* *Follow* and share."
  }
 ],
